Our client, an established farming business situated in the Ceres area, is looking to appoint a Production Manager to join their team at one of their production units.
This role is ideal for a dynamic individual looking to expand their knowledge and skills, and grow with the company. The successful candidate has excellent organisational and leadership capabilities, and will report to Farm Manager.
Responsibilities will include: *Assisting with the management of all production-related activities, from planting to harvesting *Workforce management, training, and enforcement of discipline *Implementation, monitoring, and reporting of production-related systems *Assisting in ensuring compliance with quality standards and certifications *Cost control *Recordkeeping *General farm maintenance *All other tasks related to the role.
Essential qualifications, skills, and experience:
• Matric required, a relevant tertiary agricultural qualification will be advantageous;
• Experience in fruit production, especially pome fruit and cherry production, is preferred;
• Strong communication skills (Afrikaans & English);
• Strong computer skills (MS Office);
• Valid driver’s license.
In return, our client offers competitive remuneration with housing on the farm.
Please apply online at www.m3online.co.za before 09:00 on 4 September 2026.
For general enquiries, contact our team at M3 Human Capital Management on 021 863 1444.
Please note that only shortlisted candidates are contacted. If no feedback is received within two weeks of the closing date, please assume that your application was unsuccessful.

Our client, an established water development organisation in the agricultural and commercial sector, is seeking to appoint an experienced and detail-oriented Senior Buyer to join their team based in Paarl.
The successful candidate will be responsible for managing the procurement process, sourcing goods and services, building and maintaining supplier relationships, negotiating favourable terms and ensuring the timely availability of stock and supplies. This role is ideally suited to a commercially minded individual with strong negotiation, analytical and organisational skills.
Key responsibilities include: *Manage the full procurement process, from requisition through to delivery *Source, evaluate and manage suppliers while maintaining strong professional relationships *Negotiate pricing, contracts, payment terms and delivery schedules *Analyse market trends, pricing and product quality to ensure optimal value *Work closely with internal departments to forecast demand and maintain appropriate stock levels *Monitor supplier performance and ensure agreed standards are met *Identify opportunities for cost savings, process improvements and improved procurement efficiencies *Maintain accurate purchasing records and supporting documentation *Collaborate with Finance and other relevant departments to optimise purchasing processes *Provide guidance and support to members of the purchasing team where required.
Essential minimum qualifications, skills, and experience:
• Relevant tertiary qualification in Procurement, Supply Chain Management, Business Administration or a related field;
• At least 5 years’ relevant experience in a procurement or purchasing role;
• Proven experience in supplier management and relationship building;
• Demonstrated experience in cost-saving and process improvement initiatives;
• A procurement or supply chain certification will be beneficial;
• Experience within the agricultural sector will be advantageous;
• Excellent written and verbal communication skills;
• Ability to work independently, manage multiple priorities and perform well under pressure;
• Computer literacy; experience with Sage Pastel will be advantageous;
• Fully bilingual (Afrikaans and English).
Please apply online at www.m3online.co.za before 09:00 on 3 September 2026.
For general enquiries, contact our team at M3 Human Capital Management on 021 863 1444.
Please note that only shortlisted candidates are contacted. If no feedback is received within two weeks of the closing date, please assume that your application was unsuccessful.

